From: Marco Martins
Subject: iomap: one page of zeroes for direct I/O

For a 16 MB device: the 64 KB buffer stays allocated from boot. It is only
needed for file system blocks larger than a page, which this device has none of.
---
--- a/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
+++ b/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 /*
  * Used for sub block zeroing in iomap_dio_zero()
  */
-#define IOMAP_ZERO_PAGE_SIZE (SZ_64K)
+#define IOMAP_ZERO_PAGE_SIZE (PAGE_SIZE)
 #define IOMAP_ZERO_PAGE_ORDER (get_order(IOMAP_ZERO_PAGE_SIZE))
 static struct page *zero_page;
 
